          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "Based on the Employee Handbook provided, employees receive **24 working days** of paid annual leave per calendar year. This entitlement is confirmed in the final run of the handbook, which states that every full-time employee receives 24 days of paid annual leave [1].\n\nRegarding unused days, the handbook specifies that up to 5 unused days may be carried over to the next year [1]. These unused days must be utilized before March 31st [1].\n\nAdditionally, the handbook details the travel and expense policies for business travel, which must be booked at least seven days in advance [3]. It also outlines daily limits for various expenses, such as hotel stays in Dhaka (9,000 BDT) or outside Dhaka (6,500 BDT), with meals costing 2,500 BDT per day [3].\n\nThe handbook further clarifies that claims for travel expenses must be submitted within 30 days of the trip [3]. While it mentions that receipts are required for most expenses, it notes that claims without receipts are not reimbursed unless specific exceptions apply, such as taxi fares below 500 BDT [3].\n\nRegarding probation, new employees serve a six-month probation period [4]. During this period, the notice period is two weeks, and after confirmation, it is one month [4].\n\nFor remote work arrangements, employees may work on Tuesdays and Thursdays [5]. Fully remote arrangements require written approval from the department head and are reviewed every six months [5].\n\nRegarding overtime, the handbook calculates the hourly rate as:\n$$P = 1.5 \\times (S / 160) \\times H$$\nwhere $P$ is the overtime pay, $S$ is the monthly base salary, and $H$ is the approved overtime hours [6].\n\nRegarding office hours, the Dhaka office is open from 9:00 to 17:30, with core collaboration hours being 11:00 to 15:00 [8].",
